; A TWAIN Data Source exports DS_Entry — NOT DSM_Entry, which is what a Data Source
; *Manager* exports for applications to call. TWAINDSM.dll resolves "DS_Entry" by name on
; every .ds it finds and silently skips any file that does not have it.
;
; Exported undecorated: DS_Entry is __stdcall, which on x86 would otherwise be emitted as
; _DS_Entry@20 and be invisible to the manager.
;
; Ordinal 1 as well, because some pre-2.0 managers resolve the entry point by ordinal
; instead of by name.
EXPORTS
    DS_Entry @1
